Body:
Use case: For large MCP tool outputs i want to save them to file, and instead of giving it back to agent - i want only return the structure of the output + filename and instruct it to read that file but not fully load it into context.

For this i need to hijack tool outputs using Plugins

```typescript
const LIMIT = 10_000

export const plugin = async ({ client, $ }) => ({
  'tool.execute.after': async (input, output) => {
    if (!output) return

    const mcpToolOutputFormat = output.content?.[0]?.text
    const opencodeToolOutputFormat = output.output

    const outputString = opencodeToolOutputFormat || mcpToolOutputFormat

    const tokens = outputString.length / 4 // heuristic

    if (tokens < LIMIT) return // within limit, do nothing

    // when we exceed the limit, we write the output to a file
    // and mutate the output to return a helpful message

    const filepath = writeFile(input.tool, outputString)
    const replacementMessage = `Output too big to fit into context (limit: ${LIMIT} tokens). Full output saved to: ${filepath}.`

    if (mcpToolOutputFormat) {
      // THIS IS NOT working right now because `output` in opencode was constructed this hook finished
      output.content[0].text = replacementMessage
    } else {
      output.output = replacementMessage
    }
  },
})


```

For now since it was simple I just adjusted it to handle flags, so now this works:
```
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "permission": {
    "bash": {
      "find * -delete": "deny",
      "find * -exec*": "deny",
      "find *": "allow"
    }
  }
}
```
